Falsifies `network_time_protocol::verification::parse_then_serialise_is_the_identity`.

The defect: `Packet::parse` masks the version field to two bits. A packet with the version's top bit set parses
and serialises back to a different first byte.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(p.to_bytes(), wire)`.

diff --git a/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs b/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs
index 209f6bae5..d7f0eda2f 100644
--- a/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/network_time_protocol/src/lib.rs
@@ -543,3 +543,3 @@ impl Packet {
             leap: wire[0] >> 6,
-            version: (wire[0] >> 3) & 0b111,
+            version: (wire[0] >> 3) & 0b011,
             mode: wire[0] & 0b111,
